WEBVTT

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:51.040
Spit it out. Who're you working for, bitch?

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.750
Your press pass was a fake, too.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.590
That can't be... I don't know what—

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.550
Cut the shit already! Tell us who's in charge!

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.080
Are you okay,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.080
<i>princesa</i>?

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.330
Do you know about the "Doomsday Clock"?

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:41.050
The contention between capitalist and communist blocs came to a head in 1947.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:47.050
It was then, in the beginning of the so-called "Cold War," that this clock was created to countdown

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.270
the time remaining until the end of the world.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.730
When its hands strike midnight,

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.780
the world would be destroyed, supposedly.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.740
As you can see, the small nation in
Central America named Carib is in flux.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.470
Bloodstained Vow is the revolutionary
organization that overthrew the dictatorship.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:13.280
Its leader, Fiadel Kestro, has just now appeared.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.130
Hereafter, he will head to the UN headquarters to deliver a speech,

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.740
most likely a proclamation of an independent communist nation.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.670
This is Mine Fujiko, reporting
from the capital of Carib, Nahava.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.140
My apologies. I will not
involve myself in political matters.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.900
I was told you work as an assassin.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.640
This is against my principles.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:11.370
Besides,

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.470
assassination isn't a job.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.000
Then, what is it?

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.370
It is a way of life.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.640
This woman...

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.400
Mine Fujiko?

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.330
She's just an oriental journalist,
but Fiadel seems fond of her.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.410
She's helping us in our plan this time.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.910
<i>A journalist? She's still doing these things?</i>

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.580
<i>I don't have a place to call home either.</i>

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.600
You know her?

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.510
What is it that you want?

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.760
You just have to do as I say before the UN address.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.020
It's been a while, Mr. Boyfriend.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:14.490
This is a good opportunity for the Union, Secretary General.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.880
We can threaten them by keeping Carib's nuclear missiles close-by.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.460
The first step is critical in putting a bell around the pretender's neck and keeping that new nation in check.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.630
A bell? Indeed...

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.480
Well?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.470
We've been pushing the recovery of the old regime by secretly funding its remnants.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.690
It's an alarming situation, Mr. President.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.030
It must be addressed before that
revolutionary wins over the media at the UN!

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:52.880
Carib, huh? Nevertheless, I find it hard to approve of employing an assassin.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.800
We cannot afford to delay in this situation!

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.480
Then deploy troops to Central America.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.890
I will head to the UN.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.610
It is now time to inform the world of our revolution

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.900
and join hands with those sympathetic to our cause!

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.870
Princesa! Over here.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.790
It's like you're a rock star.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.810
Timing is imperative in this kind of work.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.810
But will you be all right?

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.000
What do you mean?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.700
Hesitation cuts down your life.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:11.150
I'll remember that, Mr. Boyfriend.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.200
<i>Ms. Maria...</i>

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.050
Revolutionary leaders must sacrifice everything they have

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.150
and not expect any financial compensation.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:28.250
Only then can a true revolution come about. That's the way things work.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:29.710
That's quite idealistic.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.880
A revolution is to embrace ideals.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.800
You weren't born in Carib, but South America, right?

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.050
Why are you so dedicated to this revolution?

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:44.190
It's a pledge to the people of Carib who took me in and believed in me.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.560
And it's justice.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.450
Oh, justice, you say?

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.910
Even in Japan, Land of the Rising Sun,

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:55.490
I hear there were warriors
who fought for revolution, like us.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.540
Warriors of the Bakumatsu period?
You mean, samurai?

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.490
Yes. We... are samurai.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:08.960
Sit down! You're going to
answer some of our questions too.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:12.420
We'll undo your worthless revolution!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.080
I see... Remnants of the old regime.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.930
This is meaningless.
Even if I die, the revolution will go on.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.830
I wouldn't be so sure of that.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:26.050
We aren't the only ones
opposed to you addressing the UN.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.940
We've taken Fiadel Kestro hostage!

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.830
We have just one condition for his release!

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.260
Political asylum until our administration is restored!

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.600
Our fuel won't last.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.700
Refuel in midair!

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.700
If you don't, you'll join Fiadel in a watery grave!

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.920
If we offer you up as a present,

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.500
we'll be able to get political asylum.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.460
Are you sure?

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.470
Will it really go that well?

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.590
How's the situation?

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:02.930
We have already deployed our troops to the scene.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:05.590
The number of hijackers is unknown.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.440
It was careless to attempt an
assassination in this situation.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:35.940
I'm sorry. It looks like I've dragged
you into our struggle again.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:38.210
It's okay.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.720
More importantly, where are we headed?

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.550
I don't know.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:46.720
They're probably trying to flee to a red country. But...

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:49.660
If you understand that, then this'll be quick.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:53.160
But before that, give us the coordinates of our oil field.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.730
I see. "Our", huh?

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:01.060
I had heard a rumor that the previous regime knew of hidden oil fields in our country.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:03.260
It's not a rumor, it's the truth!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:10.000
You're mistaken. It's just a lie they fabricated to have the upper hand in negotiations.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.410
<i>You're</i> the one telling lies!

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.250
Our land's never had a valuable natural resource!

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.750
What we <i>do</i> have is ongoing construction of missile bases.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.760
In that case, you'll be coming with us.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.110
<i>Begin fueling.</i>

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.730
<i>Ready to attack.</i>

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:34.850
<i>That's...</i>

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.360
<i>I-It's them.</i>

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.390
That's the Red Stars!

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.770
I see.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.870
It looks like this situation is taking on a new dimension.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.500
There's a plane of unknown origin in the same airspace!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.120
We don't need to negotiate. Finish them off!

00:10:55.060 --> 00:11:00.840
If we allow our respective egos to clash here, it will trigger World War III.

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:06.010
If they make any suspicious moves, attack!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.680
Mister, throw it—

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:32.750
I-It's really him!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.170
Hey, here it comes! Catch!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.470
¡Gracias!

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.230
Looks like fun.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:44.200
Yeah. But to them,

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.220
baseball isn't a game.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:52.190
Only baseball and music give them a chance at living in this country.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:58.190
Ideals aren't why the world is paying attention to the revolution of such a small country.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.000
It's the worth of your hidden oil fields.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.240
I understand.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:07.450
Sometimes our duty is both glorious and unpleasant at the same time,

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.210
Mine Fujiko.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.890
And the Union is only supporting you

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:17.760
so that they can threaten their enemy by placing nuclear missile bases in their proximity.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.570
Deterrence is necessary.

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:23.140
We may be under their thumb for now,

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:27.680
but eventually, our revolution will become a wave that engulfs the whole world.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.150
Central America, South America, Eastern Europe...

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.560
Then to Asia and the Middle East.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.730
Is revolution what you're really after?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.400
Or is it chaos?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.740
I want to dance as I wish.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.580
That's all. And...

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:51.030
It's boring to just dance as a puppet state of major powers, don't you think?

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.340
Fiadel?

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.450
Won't you dance with me, princesa?

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:06.790
You seem well-informed. Are you here to find out the coordinates of the oil fields?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.100
What do <i>you</i> wish for?

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:14.600
Let's see, my wish is...

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:26.120
<i>We're ready to attack at your command!</i>

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.810
What the hell is going on?!

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:30.120
This isn't what we agreed on!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.290
You want a gunfight here?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.820
Of course not...

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.920
It looks like they've tricked us.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.750
Mine Fujiko.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.460
That's a bad habit you have with your feet.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:42.930
That's right.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:44.970
My wish is...

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.970
<i>Prepared to attack. Leave it to us.</i>

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:55.730
<i>We'll give it to those damn capitalist dogs.</i>

00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:00.440
Will they strike first or will we?
Maybe we'll have a contest of patience instead?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.540
No, we have no choice but to attack preemptively.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:07.740
The only way to survive in nuclear warfare is to annihilate the enemy!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:13.000
The one to attack first leaves behind a bad name in history. I must prevent that, at least...

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:19.000
History is meaningless if there are no humans left, Mr. President.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.460
H-Hey!

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.090
Can't you contact the fighter plane?

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.590
Which one?

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:32.560
Doesn't matter! Just stop the attack!

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:33.770
All right.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.480
This is our chance.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:42.480
What you said before about the oil fields not existing... Was that a lie?

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.440
If I announce that they don't exist in front of the UN,

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.960
it will become a fact that ensures we won't become involved in further conflict.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:56.260
You're naive. Have you forgotten that Roniania intends to store nuclear missiles in Carib?

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:57.750
You're already involved.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.310
Indeed.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:04.340
But eventually this ridiculous staring contest between two great powers will end.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:09.290
And someday the scars on
the land from this war will mend.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:13.720
After that, the thing we'll need...

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.150
Is <i>that</i> the oil field?!

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:20.270
It's an exclusive scoop. Keep it locked up tight.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.270
Why?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.650
I like to dance, you see.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:31.280
The Carib I visited in my student days was full of
beautiful beaches, great booze and exquisite women.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:34.150
It had a rhythm I liked.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.790
Is that all?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:37.860
It's enough for me.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:40.400
No matter who is pulling your strings,

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:43.790
it's better to let them have this information than have it go to those great powers,

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.050
Ms. Journalist.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.750
Since when have you known?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.530
Since we met.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:53.260
Even though I could have killed you?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.060
You were too beautiful.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.810
Princesa.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.060
Fiadel...

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.820
I don't want us to become
the trigger for World War III.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.280
They might pull that trigger.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.370
<i>Roger.</i>

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:16.790
<i>The swiftest takes the victory!</i>

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.620
<i>Missile confirmed!</i>

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.720
Th-They've opened fire!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:26.460
What?!

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.260
Preemptive attack initiated!

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.300
Th-They fired!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.760
It's the end of the world!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:40.600
<i>That's...</i>

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:42.850
<i>...a samurai?</i>

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.330
<i>A samurai cut a missile?</i>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.280
<i>Right before our eyes...</i>

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.460
<i>A samurai flew...</i>

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.780
D-Did he save us?

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.460
But... why?

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.820
Right on time.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.970
Different from the original plan, though.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.980
What's a samurai... doing in a place like this?

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:26.610
He's my boyfriend. I asked him to come get me.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:27.440
Let's go.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.610
The missiles have been destroyed!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.150
Destroyed?!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.950
World War III has been avoided!

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.560
Our preemptive missile!

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:42.640
It's not "ours." It's your independent action.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.010
Secretary General!

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.960
I don't want destruction or asylum!

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.420
Over here.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.060
Where are you taking me?

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:53.470
There's no use trying to escape!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.810
That's funny. Go ahead and shoot.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.310
What was that? What do you mean?

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:02.260
What will you do about being pawns

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:05.850
of those who don't even know the name of your country or much less care about you?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:12.190
Silence! Our actions will play out on the stage of history and change the course of the future!

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.750
Like a rock star, huh?

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:18.490
Politics isn't a play or a concert.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.740
If I kill Fiadel Kestro now, at least my name will go down in history!

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.570
If that's what you're after, why not kill The Beatles?

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:27.500
Shut up!

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:32.380
I've had enough of rock.
I prefer something with more rhythm.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:36.720
It's not time for an encore yet!

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.970
That's our ride, Comrade.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.440
Samurai...

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.640
<i>Just now, the leader of the movement which overthrew the dictatorship</i>

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:08.460
<i>of the small Central American country of Carib,</i>

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.200
<i>Fiadel Kestro, has arrived.</i>

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.580
Comrade Fiadel, everyone is waiting.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:20.220
Hear that? Listen to their cheering!

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:23.220
I see, I <i>am</i> a rock star.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.290
Yes.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.850
It will be a historic day.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.170
I've had enough of rock.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:45.720
<i>After Comrade Fiadel's talk, the lies of the previous government</i>

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:50.530
<i>about the existence of oil fields were exposed.</i>

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.120
Why didn't you assassinate him?

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:55.800
Were you scared?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.510
Hey, would you rub some suntan oil on me?

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:07.670
Leaving the underground now?

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:13.040
You didn't fulfill your task this time.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:17.310
But it's an appropriate final act since in a sense, you served justice.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.080
I don't intend to quit.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.570
Then why didn't you kill him?

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:26.920
My real aim was the location of those hidden oil fields.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:31.080
Your wish was, after all...

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.170
My wish...

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:36.460
Enough of that.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.060
I found out the location.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.550
Where is it?

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:46.170
It's here.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:52.600
As he said, what this country needed wasn't oil. So...

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:56.610
I see. So it's here.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:02.090
You want to find the place where you belong.

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:05.310
Are you in love with him?

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:08.370
Rock stars aren't my type.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.830
In that case, Maria!

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:15.100
I'm not Maria. I'm Mine Fujiko.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.090
Mr. Boyfriend.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.290
See you later.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:23.590
Mine... Fujiko.
